### Announcement API Tests

This file exercises every route of the announcement API under
`/api/announcements`: create, read (all, newest first, by author, by tags),
edit and delete. See docs/announcement-architecture.md for how the API is
built and what each route returns.

Install the **REST Client** extension in VS Code and select the `local` or
`deployed` environment. Configure the same `baseUrl`, `adminUid`, and
`adminPassword` variables used by `toolchain.http` in the Git-ignored
`.vscode/settings.json`. Never put passwords in this file.

Run the requests in order. Request 3 creates an announcement titled
"REST Client Test" and request 9 deletes it, so the run leaves no data
behind. Titles must be unique: edit and delete find an announcement by title.

### 1. Sign in (every announcement route needs a signed-in account)

# @name loginAnnouncement
POST {{baseUrl}}/authenticate
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "uid": "{{adminUid}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}

### 2. Read every announcement -> 200 with a JSON array

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/announcements
Accept: application/json

### 3. Create an announcement -> 201 with the saved announcement
# The fields are query parameters, not a JSON body.

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/announcements/create?author=REST%20Client&title=REST%20Client%20Test&body=Created%20from%20announcement.http&tags=rest-client
Accept: application/json

### 4. Read every announcement, newest first -> 200

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/announcements/orderedByTime
Accept: application/json

### 5. Read the announcement by an author -> 200, or 404 when there is none

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/announcements/author/REST%20Client
Accept: application/json

### 6. Read announcements whose tags equal a value -> 200 with an array (empty when none match)

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/announcements/tags/rest-client
Accept: application/json

### 7. Edit the body -> 200 with the edited announcement
# The new body is the plain-text request body.

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/announcements/edit/REST%20Client%20Test
Content-Type: text/plain

Edited from announcement.http

### 8. Confirm the edit -> 200 with the new body

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/announcements/author/REST%20Client
Accept: application/json

### 9. Delete the test announcement -> 204

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/announcements/delete/REST%20Client%20Test

### 10. Known issue: editing a title that does not exist -> 500, not 404

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/announcements/edit/No%20Such%20Title
Content-Type: text/plain

This request shows the current behavior described under Known issues.
